What was taken
--------------
Only the facts needed to tell a user whether a part fits on their printer:
vendor, product name, build volume, bed outline, origin offset, available
nozzle sizes, extruder count, and the nozzle_type / nozzle_hrc /
default_bed_type fields where the profile defines them. No G-code, no start or
end scripts, no motion or extrusion tuning, no filament or process settings.

Conjure does not fetch these profiles at runtime and does not bundle
OrcaSlicer's profile tree. The import is a development-time step; only the
derived JSON is committed.

