The unresolved question is whether a dataset of build volumes derived from
AGPL-3.0 profile files is a "modified version" that carries the licence
forward, or an uncopyrightable collection of facts. There is an argument each
way: individual measurements are facts and thin under Feist v. Rural
Telephone, while the compilation and its selection and arrangement may not be.
Do not assume the favourable reading.

